      "justification": "The original dictionary span, PossibleWord candidate cache, adopted matcher ownership and Southeast Asian algorithms are preserved. The equivalent Lao, Burmese and Khmer loops share a single implementation with Thai retaining its original minimum-span and suffix branches. Constructor character sets are the unchanged native UnicodeSet bounds generated from the actual pinned ICU constructors. The non-ML CJK engine now retains source dynamic-programming costs, supplementary and normalized native-index mapping, dictionary fallback, original Japanese extensions, and phrase boundary filtering. Native replay covers 712 original CJK calls across counted, deferred and UnicodeString providers. The factory now adopts all concrete dictionary engines and disposes their matchers through the original ownership boundary. The integrated build shares the ICU provider, rule data and resource dispatch with Writer, including the LibreOffice Khmer patch where selected.",
